      "title": "Truthful advertising",
      "narration": "Theo drafts a postcard for AMG’s health clients. Maryland law and MIA rules require every advertisement to be truthful and not misleading in fact or by implication. The ad must identify the insurer, describe benefits accurately, and disclose limitations, exclusions and waiting periods with the same prominence as the benefits. It may not imply that a limited policy is comprehensive, exaggerate the ease of claims, or use testimonials that are not genuine. The insurer is responsible for every advertisement used on its behalf, including the producer’s own, which is why carriers require advance approval of producer materials.",
